  "overview": {
    "title": "The green line through the desert",
    "p1": "The Draa Valley is one of Morocco’s great oasis landscapes: a long ribbon of date palms, irrigation channels and earthen villages set against bare hills and open desert.",
    "p2": "Around Zagora you can walk or drive sections of the palm grove, pass ksars and gardens, and understand why caravans needed this corridor of water and shade.",
    "p3": "Go early or late for softer light. Carry water; shade is uneven and summer heat is intense."
  },
